---
title: Pot roast
servings: 8
tags: [american, beef, braise, one-pot, weekend]
cuisine: american
time: 3 hours 15 minutes
source: Best Ever Pot Roast with Carrots and Potatoes by Little Spice Jar, https://www.littlespicejar.com/pot-roast-with-carrots-and-potatoes/
---

Heat the oven to 275°F with a rack in the centre. Season the
@chuck roast{3 1/2%lb} well on all sides with @salt{} and @black pepper{}.

Heat a #Dutch oven{} on high. Add 1 tbsp of the @olive oil{2%tbsp} and brown
the @yellow onions{2}(halved and thickly sliced) ~{3%minutes}. Lift them out.

Add the rest of the oil and the @unsalted butter{1%tbsp}. Sear the roast about
a minute on each side and lift it out.

Pour in 1 cup of the @beef broth{2-4%cups} with the @garlic{4%cloves}(minced)
and @Worcestershire sauce{2%tbsp}, scraping up the browned bits.

Return the roast and onions. Add broth until it comes halfway up the meat,
about 2 cups, and the @thyme{5%sprigs} and @rosemary{1%sprig}. Cover and bake
~{75%minutes} for a 3 lb roast, or ~{135%minutes} for 4 lb.

Add the @baby carrots{16%oz} and @Yukon Gold potatoes{1 1/2%lb}(quartered),
cover again, and bake ~{105%minutes} more, until a knife slides through
the vegetables.

Rest ~{5%minutes} before serving.
